===Etymology===
{{unc|pl}}.<ref>{{R:pl:WSEHJP}}</ref> {{displaced|pl|sl=1|niewiasta}} (now considered poetic) and {{m|pl|żona}} (meaning narrowed down to “wife”). Popularized by the Polish Romantic writers in the 19th century. {{etydate|1545}}.{{ref|{{R:pl:SXVI|+|58143}}}}
* Possibly from {{der|pl|zlw-opl|kob|t=pigpen|nocat=1}} or {{m|zlw-opl|koba|t=mare}} (the ending {{m|pl||-ieta}} is found in some contemporaneous female names (e.g. {{m|pl|Markieta}}, {{m|pl|Elżbieta}}, {{m|pl|Greta}})); however, this theory has been rejected by most etymologists.<ref>{{R:pl:Bruckner}}</ref> Compare {{m|pl|kobiałka}}.
* Boryś asserts the term is a Polish innovation with an unclear root ''kob-'' and potentially the original suffix being extended with {{m|pl|-ita}} (compare {{cog|zlw-mpl|kobita}} and {{m|pl|najmita}}), but he rejects the existence of the suffix {{m|pl||-ita}}.<ref>{{R:pl:Boryś}}</ref>
* Bańkowski asserts that the term is not native and suggests {{der|pl|gem|nocat=1}} origin, possibly a compound of {{der|pl|gmh|kobe|nocat=1||sty, shed}} (compare modern {{cog|de|Koben}}) and {{m|gmh||*geit|t=goat}} (compare modern {{cog|nl|geit}}), originally meaning “a pen for goats” but also, derogatorily, “an enclosure for service maidens”; however, he also questions why the form is ''-bie-'' and not ''-be-''.<ref>{{R:pl:Bańkowski}}</ref>
* Sławski also rejects native origin but is ultimately unable to draw connections to other languages.<ref>{{R:pl:Sławski}}</ref>
* Długosz-Kurczabowa thinks the word may be of native origin, specifically a compound of {{der|pl|sla-pro|*kobь|nocat=1||bird-flight divination}} and {{m|sla-pro|*věta||fairy}}, but she also does not reject the possibility of foreign origin, suggesting, e.g., {{der|pl|goh|gambetta|nocat=1||concubine}} or even {{der|pl|fi|kave|nocat=1||a creature related to the moon, sky, or air}} and {{der|pl|et|kabu|nocat=1||castrated animal}} (compare also {{cog|smi-pro|*kāpëk}}), as the source.<ref>{{R:pl:Poradnia PWN|Marek Łaziński|3.11.2016|https://sjp.pwn.pl/ciekawostki/haslo/kobieta;5757019.html}}</ref>

